=== Adaptor cost: NIST ML-DSA vs the LAS paper's simplified Dilithium ===
build: commit n/a branch n/a | ML-DSA-65 vs Simplified Dilithium-III (n=6, l=5, kappa=49)
protocol: 5 repetitions x 500 (sign-class) / 1000 (verify-class) iterations, mean +/- SD, same process

--- run-validity gates (a failure invalidates every timing above) ---
rejection gate [simplified Dilithium: Algorithm 1 Sign]: 2500 calls, measured 2.7300 attempts/call (acceptance 36.63%) vs exact theory 2.7188 (36.78%), 5-sigma tolerance +-0.2162 => OK
rejection gate [simplified Dilithium: Algorithm 2 PreSign]: 2500 calls, measured 2.7712 attempts/call (acceptance 36.09%) vs exact theory 2.7748 (36.04%), 5-sigma tolerance +-0.2219 => OK
rejection gate [ML-DSA: Sign (matched, no statement)]: 2500 calls, measured 5.1540 attempts/call (acceptance 19.40%) vs FIPS 204 published 5.1000 (19.61%), 5-sigma tolerance +-0.4573 => OK
rejection gate [ML-DSA: PreSign (adaptor)]: 2500 calls, measured 5.1684 attempts/call (acceptance 19.35%) vs FIPS 204 published 5.1000 (19.61%), 5-sigma tolerance +-0.4573 => OK

--- per-operation timing (us/op, mean +/- SD over 5 repetitions) ---
  operation  Simplified Dilithium-III              ML-DSA-65 ML-DSA/simp
  KeyGen              49.45 +/-  0.12         109.45 +/-  0.16      2.21x
  Sign               454.70 +/- 11.57         487.59 +/- 15.44      1.07x
  Verify             104.92 +/-  2.18         105.92 +/-  0.21      1.01x
  PreSign            466.29 +/- 21.18         510.12 +/- 17.06      1.09x
  PreVerify          106.26 +/-  0.22         110.23 +/-  0.23      1.04x
  Adapt              109.73 +/-  0.37         114.27 +/-  1.78      1.04x
  Extract             40.25 +/-  0.05          88.55 +/-  0.14      2.20x
  (ML-DSA Sign row is the MATCHED partner; stock crypto_sign_signature
   measured 476.99 +/- 13.15 us in the same run)

--- sign-class cost per ATTEMPT (rejection luck divided out) ---
                             Simplified Dilithium-III            ML-DSA-65
  Sign, us/attempt                    166.57 +/-  2.44       94.64 +/-  1.37
  PreSign, us/attempt                 168.28 +/-  0.41       98.72 +/-  1.36

--- adaptor overhead WITHIN each construction (the primary comparison) ---
  pair                       Simplified Dilithium-III            ML-DSA-65
  PreSign vs Sign (per attempt)                     1.0%                 4.3%
  PreVerify vs Verify                            1.3%                 4.1%
  Adapt vs Verify                                4.6%                 7.9%
  PreSign vs Sign (per call)                     2.6%                 4.6%
  (Extract has no basic analogue in either construction. The per-attempt
   PreSign figure is the algorithmic one; the per-call figure additionally
   carries the difference in realised restart counts, which is why the two
   can disagree in sign at this sample size.)

--- rejection sampling (counted directly, never inferred) ---
                             Simplified Dilithium-III            ML-DSA-65
  attempts/Sign                                2.7300               5.1540
  attempts/PreSign                             2.7712               5.1684

--- communication (bytes on the wire) ---
  object                     Simplified Dilithium-III            ML-DSA-65      ratio
  public key                                     4416                 1952      0.44x
  signature                                      6736                 3309      0.49x
  pre-signature                                  6736                 3309      0.49x
  statement Y                                    4416                 4416      1.00x
  witness                                         704                  640      0.91x
  swap payload (sig + Y)                        11152                 7725      0.69x

NOTE: this is a COST comparison between two engineering routes to the
same adaptor functionality. It is NOT a security comparison: the two
constructions have different parameters and different security
arguments, and neither is analysed here (out of scope).

OK: rejection gates, attempt-counter checks and success-path
    assertions all passed. Caveat: the two constructions are measured
    sequentially within one process, so intra-run drift is not
    controlled for.
